2026-08-13 version 2.1.7-web (current series):
- improvement: the "suggest players" button in invitation games now also works for WEC community admins at WEC tables they did not create themselves, just like BBC admins at BBC Step tables - the client recognises a WEC table by its exact settings, and each community keeps its own admin list
- improvement: picking the Monthly Cup or Monthly Cup Final template when creating an invitation game now fills in the real name of the current tournament - "August Cup Final" instead of the generic template name - as long as you have not typed a name of your own. The list of current titles is fetched as soon as the create page opens, so the right name is there even if you click Create right away
- bugfix: the "idle players" view of the player list no longer shows people who are watching a table - just like the desktop client, a spectator counts as being at that table, so their status light turns on and hovering their name tells you which game they are watching
- new: the table takes a night out - the Disco style sets the game in a seventies club lounge, mirror ball spinning over the dance floor, neon sign glowing behind the velvet drapes, with matching glow-tile buttons and pucks
- new: a Blacklight 4c card deck to go with it - four neon suit colours glowing on near-black cards, easy to tell apart at a glance even on a dark table
- new: a Disco card back showing the mirror ball itself, catching the blacklight colours of the deck - pick it in Settings > Styles > Card back, or it comes along automatically with the Blacklight deck
- bugfix: the automatic server update could mistake the server for empty when the only players connected were on phones with the screen momentarily off, and restart in the middle of their game - it now sees those players too and waits its turn
- bugfix: inviting a friend to a table on a home or LAN server now works as intended - the link and QR code always carried the right address, but on the friend's screen the connection form quietly fell back to its own default server, so they could not find your table. The address from the invitation now stays in place until they change it themselves
- bugfix: signing in on pokerth.net stopped working with a "version not supported" error after a server update - the way the client introduces itself has been adjusted so you can play again right away
- improvement: the web client now introduces itself to the server as its own client type, alongside the desktop and QML clients - server statistics and activity logs can finally tell web players apart
- bugfix: your avatar no longer changes identity on the server behind your back. The picture was quietly re-processed at every sign-in, and a browser update was enough to make the server treat it as a brand-new avatar - which cluttered the official avatar storage with duplicates. Your avatar is now prepared once, when you pick it, and reused exactly as is from then on
- bugfix: the Monthly Cup link in the login page menu now shows the real Monthly Cup badge - the green chip from monthlycup.pokerth.net - instead of a generic trophy
- bugfix: chat translation kept failing for some players - Google temporarily blocks addresses it sees too often, which hits VPN users especially hard. Just like the desktop client, the little globe now quietly tries a second translation service before giving up, and when nothing works at all you get a short notice instead of a silently blinking hourglass
- improvement: private conversations now belong to the account you are signed in with, just like in the desktop client - someone connecting with a different name on the same device no longer sees your messages, and yours are waiting untouched the next time you sign in. Conversations saved before this change are kept: they go to the first account that signs in after the update
- improvement: on computers, the bet keypad now opens as a small panel floating just above the action bar instead of replacing it - the buttons, the slider and the table stay exactly where they are while you type, and clicking anywhere outside the keypad simply closes it
- new: choose where bets are shown - inside the player box, in a small tray that folds out at the bottom when a player has chips in front of them (the new default on desktop, matching the official client), or next to the box as before (still the default on phones and tablets). Pick your side in Settings > Styles > Seats, "Bet display" - the change applies instantly, even mid-game
- new: the reactions window now holds 90 emojis instead of 30, organised in three pages you can flip through with the little arrows in the title bar, next to the page counter - or, on phones and tablets, simply swipe the grid left or right: faces for emotions, hands and party for the mood, and a poker page with the shark, the fish, the chicken and the whole chip rack. The window remembers which page you left open
- new: a water pistol joins the poker page and actually fires - recoil kick, muzzle flash and a tracer round zipping across, casing and all (it replaces the firecracker, which was doubling up with the bomb)
- new: a cigarette joins the break corner of the reactions window, next to the beer and the coffee, trailing lazy curls of smoke (it replaces the third sleepy emoji)
- new: the bomb has landed - pick it in the reactions window and it drops onto the table, explodes with a double shockwave and a burst of fire. Sixty other new reactions each come with their own little show: the rocket takes off, the cards flip over, the freezing face shivers, hearts thump, and the tornado spins away
- bugfix: on phones, the tabs of the About window were breaking words in the middle without a hyphen and spreading over five lines. They now stay on two lines at most, words are hyphenated properly in your language, and the lettering is slightly smaller on narrow screens so whole words fit
- improvement: on narrow screens and in languages with long words, the tabs of the About window and the labels of the create-table form now wrap onto a second line instead of being cut off with "..."
- improvement: the private message window now sends with the same little paper-plane button as the chat, right next to the text field - and after sending with the mouse, the cursor stays in the field so you can keep typing
- new: the players list now tells you where someone is playing. On desktop, rest your mouse on a player's name to read "X is playing in ...". On phones and tablets, open the player's card - the same line is written there, in your language
- new: the poker glossary is now available in all 45 interface languages. With it, all five content pages - rules, hand rankings, how to play, glossary and FAQ - are fully translated: whatever language you read the site in, every page speaks it
- new: the poker glossary is now also written in Croatian, Serbian, Catalan, Galician and Lithuanian. Thirty-five of the forty-five languages are done
- new: the poker glossary is now also written in Greek, Bulgarian, Swedish, Danish, Norwegian and Finnish. Thirty of the forty-five languages are done
- new: the poker glossary is now also written in Arabic, Persian, Hebrew and Urdu. Twenty-four of the forty-five languages are done
- new: the poker glossary is now also written in Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Japanese and Korean. Twenty of the forty-five languages are done
- new: the poker glossary is now also written in Turkish, Ukrainian, Czech, Slovak, Hungarian and Romanian. Sixteen of the forty-five languages are done
- new: the poker glossary is now also written in Dutch, Polish, Russian and European Portuguese. Ten of the forty-five languages are done
- new: the poker glossary is now written in French, German, Spanish, Brazilian Portuguese and Italian. Each entry keeps the English word - that is what comes up in the chat - and adds your own language's term next to it where one really exists
- new: the "how to play" guide is now available in all 45 interface languages, and so are the poker hand rankings. Two of the five content pages are now fully translated
- new: the "how to play" guide is now also written in Arabic, Persian, Hebrew, Urdu, Hindi, Thai and Bengali. Twenty-three of the forty-five languages are done
- new: the "how to play" guide is now also written in Dutch, Turkish, Ukrainian, Japanese, Korean, Indonesian and Vietnamese. Sixteen of the forty-five languages are done
- new: the "how to play" guide is now written in French, German, Spanish, Brazilian Portuguese, Italian, Polish, Russian and Chinese, and the links it contains keep you in the language you are reading - following "the rules page" from the French guide now opens the French rules instead of the English ones
- new: the poker hand rankings page is now available in all 45 interface languages. Whatever language you read the site in, the page speaks it - and it uses the same hand names as the game itself, so what you read there matches what you see under the table
- new: the poker hand rankings page is now also written in Swedish, Danish, Norwegian, Finnish, Czech, Slovak, Romanian and Hungarian. Thirty-one of the forty-five languages are done; fourteen to go
- bugfix: a player who walked away from a table kept their seat for ever. Every time their turn came round, the client told the server they were still there, so the inactivity timer never ran out and the chair was never freed. Seats are now released after the usual delay, exactly as with the desktop client. If you are watching a table without playing, the countdown warning will appear as it should - click OK and you keep your seat
- new: the poker hand rankings page is now also written in Vietnamese, Thai, Hindi, Bengali, Arabic, Persian, Urdu and Hebrew. Twenty-two of the forty-five languages are done
- bugfix: on the right-to-left versions of the content pages, card examples and card sequences such as A-K-Q-J-10 were being displayed back to front, which turned a worked example into a wrong one. They now always read left to right, whatever the language around them
- new: the poker hand rankings page is now also written in Polish, Russian, Turkish, Ukrainian, Chinese, Japanese, Korean and Indonesian, on top of the six languages added just before. Fourteen of the forty-five are done; the rest are on the way
- new: the poker hand rankings page is now written in French, German, Spanish, Brazilian Portuguese, Italian and Dutch, with the same hand names the game itself uses. More languages are being added
- bugfix: on the rules, hand rankings, how-to-play, glossary and FAQ pages, the links at the top always went to the English version. Reading the rules in your own language and clicking "FAQ" put you back in English. Every link now keeps the language you are reading in, whenever that page exists in it
- bugfix: when the game server refused the connection straight after answering, the client kept retrying every five seconds without ever slowing down, and the server ended up blocking the address. Retries now space themselves out properly (5s, 15s, 30s) and stop, as they were always meant to
- bugfix: the private messages window opened a little too narrow for the list of conversations on the left to be shown, so it stayed hidden even when several people had written to you. It now opens at the same size as the desktop client, and the list appears as soon as there is more than one conversation
- new: on a BBC Step table you did not create yourself, the "suggest players" button now appears if you are on the BBC admin list. It used to be reserved to whoever set the table up
- improvement: writing to a guest is now closed off, the way it is in the desktop client: the server never delivers a private message to a guest account, so the conversation stays readable but the input tells you why nothing can be sent
- bugfix: in the private messages window, the box where you type your message was squashed to the width of the Send button and pushed against the right edge, instead of stretching across the window
- new: private messages now have the same translation globe as the chat. Hover a message you received - or tap it on a touch screen - and click the globe to read it in your own language; click again to go back to the original
- improvement: the player card keeps a single button to the statistics. "Show cups" led to exactly the same window, which already contains the cups of all three rankings
- bugfix: the player card opened shorter than its own contents, so the last buttons were cut off and it had to be resized by hand every time. It now opens at the height its contents need, up to the height of your screen
- improvement: in the statistics window, your own session figures - hands played, wins, net result, last hands - now sit in their own titled card, clearly separated from the cup rankings below
- bugfix: the "Player profile" button really did nothing when clicked - the player's name was inserted into the button in a way that cut the instruction in half. It works now
- new: the "Show cups" button is back on the player card, and opens the statistics window
- improvement: statistics have moved out of the player card and into a window of their own. Clicking a name still opens the card - avatar, country, status, in-game details and the actions - while the cups of all three rankings, and your own session statistics, open in a separate window. The chart button in the players list now goes straight there
- bugfix: the "Player profile" button appeared to do nothing - the window did open, but behind the player card, which hid it completely
- improvement: your session statistics are now behind a button on your own card, like the cups, instead of being unfolded every time you open it
- bugfix: your own player card did not show your status - guest, registered or admin - while everyone else's card did. It is now shown on both, so you can check what the server actually recognised you as
- bugfix: on a wide player card, the buttons stretched across the whole window. They now keep a sensible width and stay centred - only the tables and charts use the full width
- bugfix: the player card reopened against the left edge once it had been moved or resized. It now opens in the middle every time, while keeping the size you chose
- bugfix: a first place among the last five results was unreadable in light mode - a black number on a black circle
- bugfix: on iPhone, the player card and the game info card could slide up under the status bar and the notch. They now keep clear of the safe areas
- improvement: the player card opens wider again
- bugfix: in the player card, the avatar sat against the left edge instead of being centred once the card was opened as a window
- improvement: the player card can now be widened much further - up to almost the full width of the screen - so the cup charts have all the room they need
- bugfix: the player card and the game info card now open in the middle of the screen at a comfortable size, and can actually be widened. They were stuck narrow and pinned to the top-left corner
- bugfix: the player card could not be moved in practice - the only spot that dragged it was the player's name, in the middle of the card. It now has a grip bar across the top, and it can be made considerably wider so the cup charts have room
- improvement: the player card and the game info card no longer black out the whole screen. They are ordinary windows now, like the ranking and the forum: the lobby stays readable and usable behind them, and on a large enough screen you can move them, resize them, and they reopen where you left them. Closing is done with the cross or the Escape key
- improvement: the player profile window now sizes itself to your screen instead of always opening narrow, so the placement table and the charts have room to breathe on a large display and still fit on a phone
- new: player profiles now show what the desktop client shows. A player's card has a "Player profile" button that opens a window with the current season - rank, score, average, games and points - the last five finishes, the placement breakdown with its pie and bars, the most recent games, and every past season. A season only loads when you unfold it, and seasons the player never entered simply do not appear
- bugfix: in the players list, the action icons of a row that had fewer of them than the others - your own line, or a player already at a table - slid one place to the right and no longer lined up under their column headings
- new: server admins now have the kickban hammer directly in the players list, next to the other actions, instead of having to open each player's card. The actions column widens to make room for it, and stays as it is for everyone else
- improvement: the little disk that appears while your settings are being saved to the server now sits to the left of the private messages envelope in the lobby, instead of next to the settings wheel
- bugfix: the list of players online was empty, showing only a dash, while the counter above it still announced the right number
- improvement: the private message window now looks like the one in the desktop client. Conversations are listed down the left side with the first line of the last message under each name, so a busy inbox can be read at a glance; messages appear as bubbles, yours on the right, with the time in the corner. On a narrow window the list folds into a drop-down, and with a single conversation it disappears entirely. Times show as the hour for today and gain the date for older messages
- improvement: private messages now follow the desktop client's rules exactly. While you are sitting at a running table you cannot write privately - the window closes on its own when the hand begins, and the envelope disappears from anyone already playing - so nothing can be arranged out of sight of the table. Guests, who cannot chat at all, no longer see the envelope either and are told why
- bugfix: simply opening a private message window with somebody recorded them for good, so the list at the top filled up with every player whose envelope had ever been clicked - most of them long gone from the lobby, none of them ever written to. A conversation is now created only when a message actually travels, and the empty ones left behind are cleared away on the next start. A partner who is no longer in the lobby is shown greyed out, so you know before typing
- bugfix: the private message window opened at the bottom left of the page instead of in the middle, could not be moved or resized like the ranking and forum windows, and left a stray chat bubble in the corner of the screen after it was closed
- bugfix: the column header of the players list no longer lined up with the buttons underneath it, since the envelope added a third button to a column sized for two
- new: private messages. Write to a player without the whole lobby reading along: open the envelope next to their name in the players list, or the envelope in the lobby header, and a conversation window opens. Every conversation is kept on this device and is still there the next time you come back, so a chat picked up days later carries its own history. Unread messages show as a red count on the envelope, and a bin in the window title deletes a conversation for good. The desktop client's /msg command works too - type /msg nickname your text in the lobby chat, or /msg "a nickname with spaces" your text. Messages are limited to 128 characters. A player sitting at a running table cannot be written to - you are told so before the message leaves, rather than after it has silently vanished - and if the server turns a message down for any other reason it is taken back out of the conversation instead of staying there as if it had been sent
- bugfix: translating a chat message or a forum post did nothing on an iPhone when the app had been installed to the home screen, while the same translation worked in a normal Safari tab and on a computer. The app now routes the request through the PokerTH server when the browser refuses to make it directly, so translation works again everywhere
- bugfix: translating a forum post into Chinese or Portuguese ignored your regional choice - traditional Chinese came out simplified and European Portuguese came out Brazilian. The post view now follows the same rule the chat already did
- new: the FAQ page is now translated into all 45 interface languages, like the rules page - so a search for how to play free poker in your own language finds an answer written in it
- bugfix: the Arabic, Hebrew, Persian and Urdu versions of the rules and help pages were laid out left to right, which put the punctuation on the wrong side of every sentence. They now read right to left as they should
- new: three new pages you can read without opening the app or installing anything - the poker hand rankings with examples and the odds of being dealt each one, a step-by-step guide to getting from a blank tab to a hand, and a glossary of fifty-five poker terms. They sit next to the existing rules and FAQ pages
- new: admin page - the search engine section can now refuse AI crawlers, carry your own site name, title, description and preview image, verify with Yandex, submit every page to IndexNow on demand, and run a configuration check that tells you what is set up and what is missing
- improvement: sharing a link to the poker rules or the FAQ now shows a proper preview card with a picture, the title and a summary, the way the home page already did - in Discord, WhatsApp, X or anywhere else that unfurls links
- improvement: search engines are told sooner when the site changes, and are allowed to show a full summary and a large picture instead of the short, cropped one they default to
- improvement: choosing a photo as your avatar is lighter on memory, which matters most on phones - a large picture used to be copied and held in memory twice before being shrunk, and could take the tab down with it. Pictures over 30 MB are now turned away with a clear message instead
- bugfix: the three errors you can hit when importing an avatar photo were always shown in French, whatever your language. They are now translated
- new: you can now report an inappropriate avatar. Open a player's profile and the option sits under Ignore - the same report the desktop client sends, and it lands in the same moderation queue. Available on phones too, where the desktop client offers no such menu
- improvement: emoji reactions now reach the table almost instantly. They used to be held back by about a second and a half - a safety margin set before we knew the server's real limit, which turned out to be far more generous
- bugfix: the "restore your settings" banner did nothing when you clicked Restore - the reason for the failure was shown in a message that appeared behind the banner itself, so nothing seemed to happen. The banner now says what is wrong right where you are looking: no backup file in that folder, folder access not granted, an empty or unreadable file
- new: the "restore your settings" banner shows which folder and file it is talking about, and carries a "Choose folder…" button so you can point it at the right folder - or grant access again after your browser forgot it - without going through advanced options
- bugfix: automatic backups could overwrite your backup file with an empty one before you had a chance to restore it. Writing is now held back until you either restore or dismiss the banner
- new: the "your turn" notification now carries Fold and Check/Call buttons, so you can play a hand from the notification itself without switching back to the app
- new: open with PokerTH - a style pack (.zip), a backup file (.json) or a desktop config.xml can now be opened straight from your file manager into the installed app
- new: share to PokerTH - send a style pack, a backup or a config.xml to the app from any share menu, and it is imported on arrival; an invitation link shared the same way opens the table directly
- new: invitation links now open in the installed app instead of a browser tab, including the new web+pokerth:// links
- bugfix: on the Green Casino table in light mode, the All-In button was hard to read - its label was a pale pink meant for a dark felt, while the button itself is only an outline. The label now uses the same red as that outline
- new: bet keypad on touch devices - tapping the bet amount now opens a keypad right inside the action bar instead of the system keyboard, so the table stays visible and nothing jumps around while you type. Min, 1/2, Pot and All-In are one tap away, and a small keypad button next to the field opens it on touch-screen computers too
- improvement: the bet slider is far easier to use with a finger - it now moves in the same steps as the desktop client (10, 50, 500 or 5000 chips depending on your stack) and has a much taller touch area, and dragging it no longer scrolls the page by mistake
- improvement: typing a bet amount with a keyboard now replaces the old amount instead of appending to it
- bugfix: the lobby could stay on screen, table list frozen, long after the connection had actually died - the client now notices the silence and reconnects on its own, as it already did at a table
- improvement: the server's inactivity warning now opens a proper dialog with a countdown, a sound and an "OK" button, instead of a chat line that was easy to miss - clicking OK tells the server you are still there and stops the countdown
- bugfix: losing your connection during a running game no longer cost you your seat - the client now proves to the server that the seat is yours and sits back down at the next hand, within the five minutes the server holds it. Rejoining still only works from the same device and the same browser you were playing on
- new: admin page - the shared leaderboard can now reset every week, alongside daily, monthly and yearly
- bugfix: the app sometimes offered an update that was already installed - the version marker was being read from the offline cache instead of the server
- bugfix: a newly imported seat pack only showed up after the offline cache renewed itself - the seat list is now read from the server like the table, card and music lists
- improvement: session logs - the arrow keys now move through the list, and Shift + up/down extends the selection just like Shift + click
- new: admin page - each track in the music library shows how many times players started it, and the traffic tab charts the plays of the last 14 days; nothing about who listened is recorded, and radio stations are not measured
- new: session logs - a "Select…" button lets you tick several logs and delete them in one go; on a computer you can also Ctrl (⌘) + click to pick logs one by one, or Shift + click to take a whole range
- new: custom sounds - in advanced options / sound you can now replace any game sound (fold, check, call, bet, raise, all-in, dealing, your turn, blind raises, player connected, game ready, lobby chat) with your own audio file; play it back, restore one sound or all of them at any time. Files stay in your browser and are never uploaded
- bugfix: admin traffic page - a language had one colour in the ranking and another in the per-day chart; both views now share the same colour per language
- new: admin maintenance - an "update automatically" switch: the server checks its branch every 15 minutes, puts client-only changes live at once, and waits until nobody at all is connected before anything that needs a restart
- new: the interface is now available in Swahili - 45 languages in total, help included
- improvement: the help now mentions the 45 available languages in every language
- new: the interface is now available in Bengali - 44 languages in total, help included
- new: the interface is now available in Filipino - 43 languages in total, help included
- new: the interface is now available in Thai - 42 languages in total, help included
- new: the interface is now available in Indonesian (Bahasa Indonesia) - 41 languages in total, help included
- bugfix: the "invite friends" share window opened invisibly at the bottom of the page (missing styles) - it now always appears centred on top
- new: "invite friends" now opens a share window: QR code to scan, copy button, whatsapp/telegram/e-mail/sms shortcuts, and the phone share sheet
- improvement: opening an invite link now shows which table you are invited to, right on the login screen, with the name field ready to type
- new: admin traffic page - a "show all" button expands the visitor breakdowns (all languages, systems, browsers) instead of the top-8 list
- new: admin traffic page - the language view now shows a per-day stacked chart of the last 14 days, so language trends are visible over time (history starts with this update)
- new: automatic backup - pick a folder once and the app keeps your full backup file up to date there; if the browser storage was wiped, the app offers to restore everything in one click (desktop Chrome, Edge and Opera)
- improvement: the app now asks the browser for persistent storage, so your settings, trophies and stats are protected against automatic cleanup
- bugfix: on iphone/ipad, the app installed on the home screen opened on a white screen - it now shows a dark launch screen with the pokerth logo
- improvement: the game proxy now protects itself against connection floods (per-address connection cap, silent-connection timeout) - regular play is unaffected
- new: bbc anthem table theme and matching card backside (by BaShFX)
- bugfix: "IP address blocked" when two web players joined the same table - the server used to see every web player with the proxy's address; it now receives each player's real address (PROXY protocol, active on the official server since the 2.1.7 deployment), and the ranking no longer treats all web players as one

